<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 29.96 bln levs 1- and 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 29.96 bln levs 1- and 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry sold on Wednesday two discount T-bill issues with one- and four-week maturities, yielding 3.77 percent and 17.61 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 29.957 billion levs ($10.2 million) of T-bills, and the ministry approved all of them.</p>
<p>The issues were offered with no par values or minimum acceptable prices set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3014897006	 BG3014997004</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  February 12, 1997  February 12, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    February 12, 1997  February 12, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 February 19, 1997  March 12, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 21,545.9 million levs  8,411.4 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.37 pct	    85.03</p>
<p> Bids approved		 21,545.9 million levs  8,411.4 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.37 pct	    85.03 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.77 pct	     17.61 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569 ($ = 2930 Bulgarian Levs)</p>
